[2026-09-21 14:41:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 064]   step_064: Warsaw bidirectional boundary validation -- independent
[2026-09-21 14:41:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 064]   catalogue replication of step_063.
[2026-09-21 14:41:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 064]   step_063 showed that an independent REBOUND/IAS15 integration of the
[2026-09-21 14:41:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 064]   class-1 CODE comets reproduces the catalogue's original/future boundary
[2026-09-21 14:41:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 064]   solutions to a median 0.001 deg per leg, and that the rotation-per-kick
[2026-09-21 14:41:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 064]   residual retains its cap preference after the full encounter budget is
[2026-09-21 14:41:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 064]   regressed out.  That validation was confined to a single catalogue.
[2026-09-21 14:41:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 064]   This step repeats the identical machinery on the Warsaw near-parabolic
[2026-09-21 14:41:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 064]   catalogue (Krolikowska 2014, VizieR J/A+A/567/A126): a different comet
[2026-09-21 14:41:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 064]   sample, independently determined three-leg solutions.
[2026-09-21 14:41:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 064]   For each Warsaw spike comet (0 < original 1/a < 100 x 10^-6 AU^-1,
[2026-09-21 14:41:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 064]   matching the Phase-3 spike definition) the osculating elements at the
[2026-09-21 14:41:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 064]   catalogued perihelion epoch are integrated through Sun +
[2026-09-21 14:41:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 064]   planetary-system barycentres (DE440s, REBOUND/IAS15) twice:
[2026-09-21 14:41:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 064]   backward until barycentric |r| = 250 AU  -> analogue of "original"
[2026-09-21 14:41:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 064]   forward  until barycentric |r| = 250 AU  -> analogue of "future"
[2026-09-21 14:41:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 064]   Boundary solutions are evaluated relative to the system barycentre,
[2026-09-21 14:41:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 064]   matching the catalogue's original/future convention.
